    <title>A 3D scan of Nicolas Cage’s skull was used in the 2007 film Ghost Rider.</title>
    <id>https://lzon.ca/posts/trivia/2</id>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://lzon.ca/posts/trivia/000002/"/>
    <category term="trivia" label="Trivia" scheme="https://lzon.ca/posts/trivia/"/>
    <published>2026-10-22T12:00:00Z</published>
    <updated>2026-10-22T12:00:00Z</updated>
    <author><name>Lzon</name></author>
    <content type="html" xml:base="https://lzon.ca/posts/trivia/000002/">
&lt;p&gt;For his starring roll in 2007’s Ghost Rider a full 3D scan of Nicolas Cage’s body was
taken by the special effects team. They used the scan to help create Cage’s immolated
super-hero form, including the shape of the flame-covered skull.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cbr.com/nicolas-cage-ghost-rider-secret-skull-abs-skin/&quot;&gt;https://www.cbr.com/nicolas-cage-ghost-rider-secret-skull-abs-skin/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</content>
